WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.207
Alexandria.

2
00:00:02.347 --> 00:00:06.707
Find titles fast with search and multi-dimensional filters.

3
00:00:06.847 --> 00:00:12.973
Title details bring metadata, previews, file versions and playback compatibility together.

4
00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:20.240
Explore related titles by performer, series or tags, then refine the order.

5
00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:25.240
Performer profiles connect biographies, collection insights and related titles.

6
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:30.240
Collections turn individual titles into organized themes.

7
00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:37.240
Follow the knowledge graph through performers, tags and titles to uncover connections.

8
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:42.240
Control playback position, speed, volume and playback mode in one place.

9
00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:48.240
Set start and end points, refine the range, and create highlights when ready.

10
00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:58.240
Swipe horizontally to seek. Left or right vertical swipes control brightness or volume. Double-tap left or right to rewind or advance fifteen seconds. On phones, hold for triple speed.

11
00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:02.740
Highlights retain source, duration and status for easy replay.

12
00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.740
Compare two candidates side by side to choose what to watch.

13
00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:12.007
Chat with a locally connected model in the smart curator.

14
00:01:12.147 --> 00:01:17.007
Actual model output is shown, with inference waits edited down.

15
00:01:17.147 --> 00:01:21.507
Continue the same conversation, keeping your context intact.

16
00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:26.007
Favorites, playlists and viewing history come together in your personal space.

17
00:01:26.147 --> 00:01:30.007
Understand your collection’s scale and composition at a glance.

18
00:01:30.147 --> 00:01:34.007
Yearly trends and monthly heatmaps reveal how your collection grows.

19
00:01:34.147 --> 00:01:38.273
Explore content distributions and cross-analysis to understand your collection.

20
00:01:38.413 --> 00:01:42.773
Plan storage with codec, resolution and capacity breakdowns.

21
00:01:42.913 --> 00:01:46.273
Track processing tasks and generated media assets.

22
00:01:46.413 --> 00:01:49.273
Spot missing metadata at a glance.

23
00:01:49.413 --> 00:01:57.540
Manage subtitle and speech-recognition workflows with visible progress. Speech recognition is unavailable here; automatic processing is off, with no new tasks started.

24
00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:05.040
Filter metadata by status, fill missing fields in bulk, and access filename corrections.

25
00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:10.307
Review compatibility issues and queues, then arrange processing when needed.

26
00:02:10.447 --> 00:02:15.307
Automatic ingestion preserves schedules and batch records so issues can be traced.

27
00:02:15.447 --> 00:02:18.073
Discover, watch, and organize.
